# Architecture Rules

## Naming & Paths
Follow established file/folder naming conventions:
- Use kebab-case for directories (`domain-overview`, `keyword-research`)
- Use PascalCase for component files (`BrandAuthority.tsx`, `DomainAuthority.tsx`)
- Use camelCase for hook files (`useKeywordTopics.ts`, `useDomainOverview.ts`)
- Use barrel exports (`index.ts`) for component directories

## Design System
Use pattern-library repo components only.

No inline styles/custom CSS.

## State Management
Use approved hooks/store/query; no globals:
- Use React Query (`@tanstack/react-query`) for server state
- Use `useState`/`useReducer` for local component state
- Use React Hook Form for form state
- Use Next.js `useSearchParams`/`useRouter` for URL state

## Routing
Follow existing route shapes/loaders:
- Use Next.js App Router structure (`app/(default)/[feature]/page.tsx`)
- Use `_module/` directories for feature-specific components
- Use dynamic routes with proper TypeScript interfaces
- Follow established route patterns from existing features

## Accessibility
Follow DS a11y patterns (roles, focus order, keyboard).

## i18n/Formatting
Always use shared utilities.

## Type Safety
Validate DTOs/schemas at boundaries.

## Flags & Auth
Verify ON/OFF states with feature flags.

## Analytics
Use shared event utilities with correct naming.

## Import Patterns
Follow established import conventions:
- Use barrel exports: `import { Button, Card } from "pattern-library"`
- Use path aliases: `import { Component } from "@/components"`
- Import from public surfaces only, not internal paths
- Group imports: external libraries, then internal modules
